e log names. The logs' contents were not available here. The RTL's review record is [evidence:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.e1]."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/repro_data_order_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket A: data bits must be sent LSB first", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the data-order bucket in the approved RTL [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. It sends the non-palindromic bytes 01, 80, D2, 0F and 96. It samples tx at the middle of each data bit and expects data[k] in data slot k (LSB first). It checks nothing about parity or stop length. It reads the nonce and prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict before $finish. This serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_repro_data_order"}, {"path": "tb/repro_parity_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket B: parity bit must be even parity", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the parity bucket in [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. For bytes with both even and odd counts of ones, it samples tx at the middle of the parity slot (bit 9 of the frame) and expects ^data. Data order does not move the parity slot. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the nonce. This serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_repro_parity"}, {"path": "tb/repro_frame_period_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Repro for bucket C: frame must last 11 bit periods", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the frame-period bucket in [artifact:prj-c391b404ed.design-under-investigation.a1]. For several frames, it counts the clock cycles busy stays high from the start capture and expects 11*CLKS_PER_BIT (44 at CLKS_PER_BIT=4). The count does not depend on data or parity values. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict with the nonce. This serves [requirement:req-94eee275db].", "entry": "tb_repro_frame_period"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001"], "claims": ["Bucket A (MSB-first data) is the cause of data_byte_fail.log. This is inferred from the RTL and the log 